<div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-6xl flex-col gap-6">
  <%= render FlatPack::PageTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Routes and integrations",
    subtitle: "Use the mounted proxy for profile and users-reporting URLs, with host-owned access control.",
    variant: :h1
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Mount and configure",
    subtitle: "The engine reads its configuration when the host draws routes.",
  ) %>

  <%= render FlatPack::CodeBlock::Component.new(
    language: :ruby,
    code: <<~'CODE'
      RecordingStudioUser.configure do |config|
        config.mount_path = "/recording_studio_users"
      end

      mount RecordingStudioUser::Engine => RecordingStudioUser.config.mount_path,
            as: :recording_studio_users

      recording_studio_users.profile_path
      recording_studio_users.admin_path

      mount RecordingStudioNotifications::Engine, at: "/notifications"
      mount RecordingStudioNotificationsPush::Engine, at: "/notifications/push"

      recording_studio_notifications.notifications_path
      recording_studio_notifications.settings_path
      recording_studio_notifications_push.devices_path
    CODE
  ) %>

  <p class="text-sm text-(--body-muted-content-color)">
    Profile snapshots live under the shared People root. Profile routes still identify the signed-in Devise user,
    then authorize with RecordingStudioAccessible on that Profile recording. They are not selected-root scoped.
    Devise remains responsible for authentication.
  </p>

  <%= render FlatPack::SectionTitle::Component.new(
    title: "Users reporting",
    subtitle: "A read-only, site-level RecordingStudioAdmin integration.",
  ) %>

  <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-(--surface-content-color)">
    Registration identifiers are <code>users</code> for the section, <code>recording_studio_users</code> for the
    screen, and <code>widgets.users.total</code> for the total-users widget. The reporting screen is read-only and
    gated by RecordingStudioAccessible through the host's configured admin access recording.
  </p>
</div>
